  "body": "Add a shop tester kit for Okuma OSP-P300M / OSP-P500 mills, following `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/README.md` and `crates/app/tests/microarc_test_part.rs`. Build this after the core post (#1964) and GENOS machine files (#1967).\n\n## Requirements\n- Create `docs/tester-kits/okuma-osp/README.md` with clear, safety-first air-cut steps (verify in OSP simulation or dry-run first, raise Z work offset above fixture, run first pass in single-block mode with feedrate override low).\n- Add a small test part covering facing, pocket/contour arcs (`G02`/`G03` `I`/`J`), spot/peck drill (`G71 Z`/`M53`, `G81`/`G83`), rigid tap (`G284`), and coolant switches (`M08`/`M51`/`M09`).\n- Commit the generated `.camproj` and golden `.min` file inside `docs/tester-kits/okuma-osp/`.\n- Add `crates/app/tests/okuma_test_part.rs` (using the `microarc_test_part.rs` `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` pattern) to build the project through app commands and assert byte-exact `.min` output.\n- Include a short hardware feedback checklist for the operator (program load `.MIN`, `G20`/`G21` unit behavior, `G15 H1`, `G56 H`, `T<n> M06` active-tool behavior, `G71`/`M53`, `G284`, `M50`/`M51`/`M59`, and safe Z retract).\n\nDone means: `docs/tester-kits/okuma-osp/` holds the README, project, and golden `.min` file, and `okuma_test_part.rs` builds and verifies the posted `.min` bytes clean.\n\nPart of #1959\n",
